ration to true, preventing the focus trap from activating. Consequently, pressing Tab a second time moves focus outside the panel to the amount field.","repair_strategy":"Remove the data-bs-scroll=\"true\" attribute from the offcanvas element so that the scroll option defaults to false, allowing the focus trap to activate and keep focus inside the offcanvas when tabbing.","edits":[{"path":"index.html","sha256":"60f9c30eaf2574c405d38683a298cad18c74b612a5860995a330a93d1aec35fc","before":"  <div class=\"offcanvas offcanvas-end\" data-bs-scroll=\"true\" data-bs-backdrop=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\" id=\"help\" aria-labelledby=\"help-title\">\\n","after":"  <div class=\"offcanvas offcanvas-end\" data-bs-backdrop=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\" id=\"help\" aria-labelledby=\"help-title\">\\n"}],"expected_accessibility_effect":"Focus remains trapped inside the offcanvas panel when tabbing; the second Tab press keeps focus on the #help-close button (or cycles to the first focusable element) instead of moving to the amount field outside the panel.","functional_risks":["Removing data-bs-scroll=\"true\" may change scrolling behavior when the offcanvas is open; however, the offcanvas is narrow and unlikely to require body scrolling, so the impact is minimal."],"verification_requirements":["After opening the help panel with Enter, pressing Tab once should focus the #help-close button.","Pressing Tab a second time should keep focus inside the panel (either on #help-close or loop to the first focusable element).","Verify that the offcanvas content can still be scrolled internally if needed."]},"provenance":{"provider":"Nebius Token Factory","model":"nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b","requestId":"chatcmpl-04fa5f67b02aa2238089260d4e787b45","promptHash":"ba66998b786f8f59736d77008eb1c5586335782b772db68cafb69c5e405ba7eb","schemaVersion":2,"structuredOutput":false,"latencyMs":13147,"usage":{"completion_tokens":2646,"prompt_tokens":15032,"total_tokens":17678,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_p